## Purpose
T003 may already have been claimed or underway when its body was appended with the NAS dogfood coordination note for B369/B370. Independently recheck the final T003 result against that update rather than assuming its executing agent saw it.

## Required review
- Read the complete current P9.M2.E1.T003 including the NAS dogfood follow-up, its final evidence/receipts, and B369/B370.
- Verify the update was explicitly considered: generic grant-aware send/connector changes are coordinated in one serial integration lane, and the existing draft contact-deliver-client commit is accounted for if relevant.
- Confirm NAS/private-relay tests were not substituted for T003 required production public-relay proof, and that changed source/generated artifacts invalidate old exact-source build/install receipts as specified.
- Record which B369/B370 changes actually landed before the reviewed candidate and which remain pending; do not require unrelated pending bugs to complete just to close this review.
- If T003 missed the appended requirements or its completion claims exceed evidence, report precise gaps and reopen/create scoped follow-up work without discarding valid earlier evidence or touching unrelated live agents.

## Acceptance
A review receipt explicitly cites the appended note, exact T003 candidate/source identity and relevant validation evidence, gives PASS or concrete gaps, and records any corrective backlog IDs. Task existence is not proof T003 was rechecked. Preserve existing T003 claims/history; perform this follow-up after T003 completion.